;; THE PRICE TABLE — what a model's tokens cost, so GET /v1/runs/:id can put
;; dollars (:cost) beside the tokens (:usage). Read by samizdat.pricing.
;;
;; US dollars per MILLION tokens, by model id as the run records it (the
;; runs.model column, side_calls.model), and optionally by provider name as
;; well, for one model priced differently by two endpoints:
;;
;;   {:models    {"model-id" {:input 0.0 :output 0.0
;;                            :cache-read 0.0 :cache-write 0.0}}
;;    :providers {"provider" {"model-id" {:input 0.0 :output 0.0}}}}
;;
;; :input and :output are required; a missing cache rate bills those tokens at
;; :input. A provider's entry is the price whole, not merged with the model's.
;;
;; LAYERED like config.edn: $SAMIZDAT_PRICING_FILE > .samizdat/pricing.edn >
;; the profile's or ~/.config/samizdat/pricing.edn > this file, deep-merged,
;; and config.edn's :pricing (same shape) over all of them. Add your own
;; providers' rates there.
;;
;; EMPTY ON PURPOSE. A price is a fact about a vendor's current rate card, and
;; nothing in this repository records one; a number written here from memory
;; would be a guess presented as a bill. A model without a price is listed
;; under :cost :unpriced and never estimated.
{:models {}
 :providers {}}
